language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Schedule tasks that share one renewable resource and respect precedences, finishing as early as possible.
given n_tasks, n_prec : int(1..)
given capacity : int(1..)
given dur, demand : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_tasks)] of int(0..)
given prec : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_prec), int(1..2)] of int(1..n_tasks)
$ no schedule needs longer than all tasks one after another
letting horizon = sum(dur)
find start : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_tasks)] of int(0..horizon)
find makespan : int(0..horizon)
branching on [start]
heuristic sdf
minimising makespan
such that
$ every task ends by the makespan
forAll t : int(1..n_tasks) . start[t] + dur[t] <= makespan,
$ a task starts only after each of its predecessors has finished
forAll k : int(1..n_prec) . start[prec[k, 1]] + dur[prec[k, 1]] <= start[prec[k, 2]],
$ at no time do running tasks use more than the capacity
cumulative(start, dur, demand, capacity),
$ implied: the work must fit under the capacity before the makespan
makespan * capacity >= (sum t : int(1..n_tasks) . dur[t] * demand[t])
